ºDestruction and death say,¦layout ‚¤textÙ-We have heard the fame thereof with our ears.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ"God understandeth the way thereof,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And he knoweth the place thereof.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ(For he looketh to the ends of the earth,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And seeth under the whole heaven;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ!To make the weight for the winds;¦layout ‚¤textÙ&And he weigheth the waters by measure.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#When he made a decree for the rain,¦layout ‚¤textÙ+And a way for the lightning of the thunder:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#Then did he see it, and declare it;¦layout ‚¤textÙ)He prepared it, yea, and searched it out.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textµAnd unto man he said,¦layout ‚¤textÙ-Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ)And to depart from evil is understanding.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse